.TH "C3L" "1" "2026-01-22"
.P
.SH NAME
.P
\fBc3l\fR - a library manager for C3 projects.\&
.P
.SH SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBc3l\fR [\fB-h\fR] [\fB-v\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [ \fIARGS\fR ]
.P
.SH DESCRIPTION
.P
\fBc3l\fR is a \fBlibrary manager for C3 projects\fR.\& It streamlines the process of
fetching, updating, and managing C3 libraries from remote repositories.\& With
c3l, all metadata about your libraries is tracked in a simple `.\&c3l.\&deps` file,
making maintenance and versioning of your project dependencies effortless.\&
.P
Some relevant dependency information—including name, source URL, current version
or tag—is stored in a `.\&c3l.\&deps` file at your project root.\& This enables easy
auditing of all dependencies in use and als a clean removal and easy updating of
the libraries.\&
.P
.SH COMANDS
.P
\fBfetch\fR \fIrepo_url\fR [ \fItag\fR ]
.RS 4
Fetch a C3 library from a git repository at \fIrepo_url\fR.\& An optional
\fItag_name\fR can used to fetch a specific version.\& Note that this allows
the \fBupdate\fR command to work properly.\&
.P
\fBfetch\fR will update the '\&dependency'\& entry in \fIproject.\&json\fR.\& It will
also create a new entry in the \fI.\&c3l.\&deps\fR.\&
.P
See also \fILOCALREPO\fR for using a
locally stored repository.\&
.P
.RE
\fBupdate\fR \fIrepo_name\fR
.RS 4
Update the library to the newest tagged release, updating the metadata in
\fI.\&c3l.\&deps\fR and \fIproject.\&json\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fBremove\fR \fIrepo_name\fR
.RS 4
Remove the library \fIrepo_name\fR and also update \fIproject.\&json\fR and
\fI.\&c3l.\&deps\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fBpull\fR
.RS 4
Pull all the fetched libraries from the .\&c3l.\&deps file.\& Use
this command when only the .\&c3l.\&deps file is in the repo but
not the libraries and you want to pull all the dependencies.\&
.P
.P
.RE
\fBlist\fR
.RS 4
List all installed libraries that are stored in \fI.\&c3l.\&deps\fR.\&
.P
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.P
Fetch a C3 library and use it (note the difference between \fBc3c\fR and \fBc3l\fR):
.P
.nf
.RS 4
c3c init app
cd app
cat <<EOF > src/main\&.c3
import encoding::hex;
fn void main() => (void)hex::dump_bytes("C3 is great");
EOF
c3l fetch http://github\&.com/konimarti/hex\&.c3l
c3c run
.fi
.RE
.P
Remove a C3 library:
.P
.nf
.RS 4
c3l rm hex\&.c3l
.fi
.RE
.P
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.P
\fILOCALREPO\fR
.P
.RS 4
Set \fILOCALREPO\fR to a folder which contains the sources of a C3 library.\&
This will prevent \fBc3l\fR from using \fBgit clone\fR.\&
.P
Example:
.nf
.RS 4
LOCALREPO=\&.\&./hex\&.c3l c3l fetch http://github\&.com/konimarti/hex\&.c3l
.fi
.RE
.P
.RE
\fIDEBUGC3L\fR
.P
.RS 4
Set \fIDEBUGC3L\fR to print all executed Bash statements.\&
.P
Example:
.nf
.RS 4
DEBUGC3L=1 c3l list
.fi
.RE
.P
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.P
